  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "research_question": "To characterize the clinical presentation, microbiological profile, and environmental spread of a Salmonella infection within a canine breeding facility.",
      "study_design": "A descriptive case report and outbreak investigation utilizing clinical observation, sample collection, and laboratory diagnostics.",
      "population_setting": "A Bulgarian Rottweiler breeding kennel comprising adult and post-partum dogs.",
      "main_findings": "Affected animals exhibited gastrointestinal symptoms and lethargy, with more severe presentations occurring in recently whelped females. Microbiological testing revealed extensive bacterial shedding among the dogs alongside contamination of their diet and surrounding surfaces. Full recovery followed the cessation of raw diet administration, implementation of targeted drug therapy, and thorough sanitation, while exposed humans remained uninfected.",
      "public_health_relevance": "The report highlights the cross-species transmission potential of pathogens found in unregulated raw animal feed. It advocates for enhanced feed traceability and biosecurity standards to mitigate health threats under a collaborative veterinary-human health approach.",
      "limitations": "The evaluation relies on observational data from a single facility without a comparative control cohort. Consequently, the observed outcomes may not reflect broader canine populations or different regional conditions.",
      "gids_interpretation": "This article contributes to the academic record of veterinary infectious disease events and diagnostic methodologies. Its documentation aids scholarly monitoring of dietary-related microbial risks in domestic animal settings.",
